# Vercel Speed Insights Integration Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project.

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- **Framework**: React 19.2.5 with Vite 8.1.4
- **Package Manager**: npm (package-lock.json present)
- **TypeScript**: Enabled with TypeScript 7.0.2

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies (253 packages added)

#### 2. Code Integration
Modified `src/main.tsx` to integrate Speed Insights:
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component within the StrictMode wrapper
- Component placed after the main FruitList component to ensure proper initialization

#### 3. Files Modified
- `My-React-Website/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `My-React-Website/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependencies
- `My-React-Website/src/main.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component

### Implementation Approach
Following the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), the React/Vite-specific instructions were applied:
- Used the `/react` export from `@vercel/speed-insights` package
- Placed the component at the root level in main.tsx for app-wide coverage
- No additional configuration required - the component works out of the box

### Verification
✅ Build successful: Project builds without errors using `npm run build`
✅ TypeScript compilation: No TypeScript errors
✅ Dependencies installed: All 253 packages successfully installed
✅ Lock file updated: package-lock.json properly updated

Note: Pre-existing linting errors were found in server files (server/db.js, server/index.js) but these are unrelated to the Speed Insights integration.

### Next Steps for Deployment
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights → Enable)
3. After deployment, the Speed Insights tracking will automatically collect performance metrics
4. View metrics in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights section

### Technical Notes
- Speed Insights will only collect data in production environments
- The component is lightweight and won't impact development performance
- No additional configuration is needed - metrics are automatically sent to Vercel
- The integration follows React/Vite best practices by placing the component at the root level
